{number: 63}
{title: Give of Your Best to the Master}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Give of your best to the Master;
Give of the strength of your [Bb7] youth;
Throw your [Eb] soul’s fresh, glowing ardor
Into the battle for [Bb7] truth.
[Eb] Jesus has set the example,
Dauntless was He, young and [Ab] brave;
Give [Eb] Him your loyal devotion;
Give Him the [Bb7] best that you [Eb] have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb] Give of your best to the Master;
Give of the strength of your [Bb7] youth;
Clad in [Eb] salvation’s full armor,
Join in the [Bb7] battle for [Eb] truth.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Give of your best to the Master;
Give Him first place in your [Bb7] heart;
Give [Eb] Him first place in your service,
Consecrate every [Bb7] part.
Give, [Eb] and to you will be given;
Held His beloved Son [Ab] free;
Grate-[Eb] fully seeking to serve Him,
Give Him the [Bb7] best that you [Eb] have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Give of your best to the Master;
Naught else is worthy His [Bb7] love;
He [Eb] gave Himself for your ransom,
Giving up glory a-[Bb7] bove:
Laid [Eb] down His life without murmur,
You from sin’s ruin to [Ab] save;
Give [Eb] Him your heart’s adoration,
Give Him the [Bb7] best that you [Eb] have.
{end_of_verse}
